his morning. Both had their latest release go bad right after a healthy one. Since a rollback changes production and opening an incident pages on-call, I didn't want to guess.\n\nHow do you want to proceed?\n1. **Roll back both**: `payments-api` to v5.0.0 and `payments-worker` to v3.3.0, then open one SEV2 incident covering both. Both rollbacks go to versions that were healthy before, so neither needs change-manager approval.\n2. **Roll back one**: tell me which service went out this morning, and I'll roll back only that one and open the SEV2 for it. One service's errors may just be fallout from the other's.", "type": "text"}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01HvQc5tkiqUjpFfhUE2qzyd", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker", "version": "v3.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01D11cMR2nWALb7XZr317wDC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "payments-worker v3.4.0 errors after deploy; rolled back to v3.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-worker", "summary": "After this morning's deploy of payments-worker v3.4.0, the service went unhealthy with an 18% error rate in us-east, us-west and eu-west. payments-api (v5.1.0) is also degraded at an 18% error rate, which we believe is downstream of the worker. payments-worker has been rolled back to v3.3.0, its last version that was healthy in production. Next: confirm the worker recovers and that payments-api error rates return to normal.", "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Rpck9hRmuzSDswN9j6f2P3", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01PZRpDrd5eZVWNZwUWHn1Rc", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled back `payments-worker` to v3.3.0 and opened the SEV2. The worker has recovered, but `payments-api` is still failing.\n\n- **Rollback:** `payments-worker` went from v3.4.0 to v3.3.0, its last version that was healthy in production, in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It's now healthy, with its error rate down from 18% to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** I opened **INC-0001** (SEV2, `payments-worker`), and on-call has been paged. The incident notes say the API errors are thought to be downstream of the worker.\n- **Still failing:** `payments-api` (v5.1.0) is still unhealthy at an 18% error rate. It may just need time to recover, for example to clear a backlog or reconnect. But if it doesn't improve, its own v5.1.0 release could be part of the problem. Its last version that was healthy in production is v5.0.0.\n\nI haven't changed `payments-api`. If its error rate stays high, I can roll it back to v5.0.0 (no approval needed, since that version was healthy before) and add it to INC-0001.", "type": "text"}]}]}